From: WinBoat
Subject: [PATCH] d3d10umd: a failed resource creation reports out-of-memory

CreateResource checked the wrapper (pResource, never NULL) instead of the gallium resource after resource_create,
so a resource the winsys couldn't allocate (the kernel driver's GPU memory limit, for one) went on as NULL and the
program crashed. Now the runtime gets E_OUTOFMEMORY, and CreateTexture2D and friends fail as on a full graphics card.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
index 03b2579..aa00670 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/d3d10umd/Resource.cpp
@@ -343,7 +343,7 @@ CreateResource(D3D10DDI_HDEVICE hDevice,                                // IN
    }
 
    pResource->resource = screen->resource_create(screen, &templat);
-   if (!pResource) {
+   if (!pResource->resource) {
       DebugPrintf("%s: failed to create resource\n", __func__);
       SetError(hDevice, E_OUTOFMEMORY);
       goto unlock;
